# Build context exclusions.
#
# Two of these are correctness issues, not just speed:
#
#   • node_modules — every Dockerfile here installs dependencies in an Alpine
#     stage and then runs `COPY . .`. Without this line that copy would overwrite
#     the freshly installed Linux modules with the host's, so a Windows or macOS
#     developer would build an image containing native binaries (Prisma's query
#     engine, @node-rs/argon2) that cannot load on Linux.
#   • .env — secrets. A file copied into any layer stays in the image even if a
#     later layer deletes it, and the real values arrive as runtime environment
#     variables anyway.

node_modules
**/node_modules

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Build output. Stale artefacts from a host build must not shadow the in-image
# build, and .next in particular is regenerated by the builder stage.
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo

# Test and tooling output
coverage
**/coverage
test-results
**/test-results
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
blob-report
**/blob-report
.playwright
**/.playwright

# Local data that must never end up in an image
uploads
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docker's own files
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
